  "summary": "Bidriware is a metal handicraft from the city of Bidar in Karnataka, India.",
  "description": "Bidriware is a metal handicraft from the city of Bidar in Karnataka, India. It was developed in the 14th century C.E. during the rule of the Bahmani Sultans. The term \"bidriware\" originates from the township of Bidar, which is still the chief center of production. The metal used is white brass that is blackened and inlaid with silver. As a native art form, Bidriware obtained a Geographical Indications (GI) registry on 3 January 2006.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Karnataka; registration 2004–05), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
